  <p class="lead">The held-out v2 pages degraded the way hospital scans and faxes are: blur, low resolution, heavy compression,
    skew and 1-bit fax. Same pixel-level scoring; the ground-truth boxes follow the transformation.</p>
  <div class="grid2" style="grid-template-columns:1.35fr 1fr;align-items:start">
    <div class="card" style="background:#fff">
      <h3>Recall: rules only vs. full RedactAgent</h3>
      {% for r in robust %}
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:190px 1fr 58px;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin:5px 0;font-size:13px">
        <div><b>{{ r.label }}</b>{% if r.level %} <span style="color:#5b6478">&middot; {{ r.level }}</span>{% endif %}</div>
        <div style="position:relative;height:18px;background:#eef1f8;border-radius:4px">
          <div style="position:absolute;left:0;top:0;height:8px;width:{{ r.A*100 }}%;background:#a5adc0;border-radius:3px"></div>
          <div style="position:absolute;left:0;top:9px;height:9px;width:{{ r.D*100 }}%;background:{{ '#1f3a8a' if r.kind != 'clean' else '#be185d' }};border-radius:3px"></div>
        </div>
        <div style="text-align:right"><b>{{ "%.1f"|format(r.D*100) }}%</b></div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
      <p class="note" style="margin-top:6px">Grey: rules only (regex / DLP baseline). Blue: full system with the agentic check.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="card"><h3>What it shows</h3><ul>
        <li><b>Fax, compression and skew</b> barely matter: within the run-to-run variation (&plusmn;1 point).</li>
        <li><b>Blur and low resolution</b> cost 3&ndash;5 points: characters merge, OCR misreads digits.</li>
        <li>The language and vision layers recover what the rules lose on every degraded set.</li></ul></div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:12px"><h3>In deployment</h3><p>The unread-ink check flags regions the OCR could not read, and those pages are
        sent to full review. A scanner setting of &ge;&nbsp;150&nbsp;DPI is the one hard recommendation.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
